      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please double check my analysis: we can determine the list of `aom_image_t` struct members the encoder ignores by first analyzing the following code in the `encoder_encode()` function in av1/av1_cx_iface.c:\n\n```\n      YV12_BUFFER_CONFIG sd;\n      res \u003d image2yuvconfig(img, \u0026sd);\n      // When generating a monochrome stream, make |sd| a monochrome image.\n      if (ctx-\u003ecfg.monochrome) {\n        sd.u_buffer \u003d sd.v_buffer \u003d NULL;\n        sd.uv_stride \u003d 0;\n        sd.monochrome \u003d 1;\n      }\n```\n\n`encoder_encode()` won\u0027t use `img` (except to test whether `img` is a null pointer) after that point.\n\nThen, we analyze how the local variable `sd` is used. You will see that the following fields of `sd` are not used:\n* color_primaries\n* transfer_characteristics\n* matrix_coefficients\n* chroma_sample_position\n* color_range\n\nHowever, the `monochrome` field of `sd` is used. But because we set `sd.monochrome` to 1 if `ctx-\u003ecfg.monochrome` is 1, I think we should say that `img-\u003emonochrome` can be 0 or 1 if `ctx-\u003ecfg.monochrome` is 1, but `img-\u003emonochrome` must be 0 if `ctx-\u003ecfg.monochrome` is 0. Sigh.",
      "revId": "16f1c458c4ca646e9b81713a4ed1aec5bcad8b59",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
